From ea46e19203dd3c4f88eaa66ec045667a253b4fea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:31:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: track workload reclaim targets and release quota as
 stopped workers terminate

When partial preemption shrinks a workload, Kueue must not immediately release quota while surplus worker pods are still running or terminating, nor should it allow newly created pods to ungate above the reclaim target. Conversely, once stopped worker pods terminate, the freed quota must be released back to the ClusterQueue without waiting for the full workload slice to finish.

Introduce reclaim target tracking in the workload and elastic job ungater controllers. Cap ungating at the target counts, mark stopped pods reclaimable in the Workload status once they terminate, and reconcile in-place scale-downs so that autoscaler adjustments below or up to admitted counts preserve correct quota accounting.
